# TechTonic Code Style (V2.0)

## Layout (post Phase 1)

- Routes & global layout: `src/app/` only.
- Shared hooks: `src/hooks/` → `@/hooks/...`
- Utils & content: `src/lib/` → `@/lib/...`
- 3D (transitional): `src/components/3d/` → `@/components/3d/...`
- Legacy page UI: root `components/` until Phase 2 migration — do not add permanent modules there.
- New code under `src/`; use `@/` alias. Edit `src/` copies, not removed duplicate roots.

## TypeScript

- Strict mode; avoid `any` (warn if unavoidable, isolate and document).
- Prefer `interface` for shared contracts; place in `src/types/` or feature models.
- Use `import type` for type-only imports.

## React / Next.js

- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for interaction or browser APIs.
- Thin route files; business logic in hooks/services.
- Co-locate feature hooks with their feature (Phase 2+).

## Naming

- Files/folders: `kebab-case`. Components: `PascalCase`. Hooks: `use*` (`use-timeline.ts` for new files).

## Architecture

- Respect `ARCHITECTURE.md` and `PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md`.
- No cross-feature deep imports; no circular dependencies.
- Official copy in `lib/content/*` — no long hardcoded strings in components.

## Security & performance

- External `_blank` links: `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- 3D: lazy-load heavy scenes, cap DPR, respect `prefers-reduced-motion`, canvas decorative only — critical content in HTML.
- Validate inputs at boundaries.

## Quality gates (local)

```bash
npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run build
```

Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject` — see `CONTRIBUTING.md`.
